.env
venv/
datasets/*
# The deploy image (Dockerfile.render, DATA_BACKEND=memory - see
# server/app/services/data_store.py) copies these three straight from the
# repo, so they need to be tracked; everything else under datasets/ (raw
# scrapes, models, html, etc.) stays ignored.
!datasets/enriched_descriptions/
!datasets/cleaned_reviews/
!datasets/route_geometry/
# The deploy image also bakes in the one trained model the API serves
# (condition_models.joblib, ~1.3MB) so no S3 bucket is needed at runtime.
# Only that file - models/ also holds a 424MB random-forest variant that
# must stay out of git and out of the image.
!datasets/models/
datasets/models/*
!datasets/models/condition_models.joblib
